---
name: dev-sanity-task
version: 2.20.1
description: lead sanity check assignment for the member that fills the dev-sanity role (resolve-role dev-sanity). task_id is the sanity check bead. The member splits the checked bead per numbered deliverable (sanity-split), runs LLM and JEV checkers per deliverable and a selected merge with lint alongside, then reports PASS or FAIL. Not QA.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - checked_bead
  - sprint
  - worktree_path
  - base
  - pr_url
  - primary_checkout
  - lint_command
  - beads_dir
  - close_context
defaults:
  sanity_close_mode: "legacy"
  qa_task_id: ""
  sanity_task_id: ""
  dev_task_id: ""
  pr_number: ""
  commit: ""
  branch: ""
  layer_prs: []
metadata:
  type: dev-sanity-task
  tags:
    - stage:dev-sanity
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: dev-sanity-start
    stage: dev-sanity
    transition: start
---
{% set task_id = sanity_task_id if sanity_task_id else task_id %}
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" mode="dev-sanity" close-mode="{{ sanity_close_mode }}">
  <description><![CDATA[Sanity check `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`: each numbered deliverable is written; lint passes. This is not QA.]]></description>

  <checked-bead><![CDATA[{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}]]></checked-bead>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <base><![CDATA[{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}]]></base>
  <layer-prs><![CDATA[{{ layer_prs | join(" ") | string | cdata_escape }}]]></layer-prs>
  <pr number="{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}"><![CDATA[{{ pr_url | string | cdata_escape }}]]></pr>
  <lint-command><![CDATA[{{ lint_command | string | cdata_escape }}]]></lint-command>
  <beads-dir><![CDATA[{{ beads_dir | string | cdata_escape }}]]></beads-dir>
  <close-context><![CDATA[{{ close_context | tojson | cdata_escape }}]]></close-context>
  <workflow>
{% if sanity_close_mode == "daemon" %}
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Export BEADS_DIR={{ beads_dir | string | cdata_escape }}. At task_ready, run atm task start {{ task_id }} "Check each numbered deliverable" and claim with bd update {{ task_id }} --claim --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY". Use the current bead relationship and worktree to identify the dev's implementation. Required planning fields are enforced by bd-validation; do not add a commit-freeze gate or manual dispatch checklist. An assignment conflict or failed verification command must be escalated to the phase lead with the exact records/error and recovery action; never wait silently. Produce the selected-result JSON in step b. No split manifest is required and no build-running split/merge helper may run.]]></step>
{% else %}
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Export BEADS_DIR={{ beads_dir | string | cdata_escape }}. Run {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/assignment-gates.py sanity --bead {{ task_id }} --commit {{ commit }} --worktree {{ worktree_path }}. Do not run a separate bd ready or bd show. READY: claim with bd update {{ task_id }} --claim --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY", then atm task start {{ task_id }} "Check each numbered deliverable". NOT_READY: diagnose with bd show {{ task_id }} --json and bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'; for each reported blocker run bd show <blocker> --json. Do not claim or start. Close refused with task-refused.md.j2, bead_state open, and reason_md naming the bead, the blocker or status, who must move it, and any missing edge bd dep add {{ task_id }} --blocked-by <blocker>. GATE_CANNOT_RUN: close refused with the exact gate command and failure evidence in reason_md; leave the bead open. Do not run bd ready separately. Copy <close-context> unchanged to scratch/close-context.json; pass it to sanity-split with --close-context. The split manifest carries all close fields and bead notes; never build or edit close vars by hand.]]></step>
{% endif %}
{% if sanity_close_mode == "daemon" %}
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Verify the numbered deliverables and the dev's existing build/test evidence for the implementation being reviewed. Inspect only each PR in <layer-prs> using its baseRefOid...headRefOid diff; if empty, use the single range from <base> to the current implementation head. Record the observed commit for evidence provenance; it is not a planning pin or a close prerequisite. Sanity does not build: do not invoke Cargo, the lint or test commands, or a split/merge helper that launches them. Preserve completed review reports. Missing or stale dev evidence is a FAIL item for the dev, but only after reading the evidence the dev supplied (completion report, linked logs, final-tree manifest); scoped checks after a rebase that the quality policy allows count, and a full-suite run on the final head is not required. Produce the selected-result JSON with task_id={{ task_id }}, reviewer=sanity-selected, a nonempty run_id, verdict PASS or FAIL, and findings as an array of {deliverable: <number>, issue: <reason>}; use deliverable 0 for a verification-wide evidence deficiency. PASS requires no findings; FAIL requires at least one. Include findings_md and lint_md describing only evidence actually inspected. If a conflicting assignment prevents identifying the target, a required review service is unavailable, or a verification tool fails, escalate the concrete conflicting records or failed operation/error to the phase lead. Do not fabricate a verdict or substitute CANNOT_RUN.]]></step>
{% else %}
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Follow `.claude/agents/dev-sanity.md`, the canonical coordinator. Run sanity-split once, with `--layer-pr <n>` for each PR in `<layer-prs>` (empty: the single range from `<base>`), and send identical assignments to both reviewers concurrently. Keep both raw result arrays; a JEV reply's `data.jev` comes only from `wrap_jev_receipt.py`. When a reviewer's last reply or timeout envelope arrives, record its completion epoch before merging or waiting for shared lint, then merge it immediately with `--started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch>`. Append no history until selected merge sets the final verdict. Build one strict selection array, one entry per deliverable; record the selected start epoch when selection begins and completion epoch when `selection.json` is written. Invoke selected merge only as `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/sanity-merge ... --reviewer sanity-selected --started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch> --llm-vars <sanity-llm-vars.json> --jev-vars <sanity-jev-vars.json> --selection <selection.json>`; it ignores stdin. Append history in exact order `sanity-llm`, then `sanity-jev`, both rows with the selected verdict as `--final-verdict`; if selection or selected merge cannot run, use `CANNOT_RUN` and still append LLM/JEV. Retain selected vars unchanged as the --vars input to atm task close; the daemon hook resolves task and bead context. Exit 4: wait for shared lint; retries reuse supplied epochs. Selected cannot-run routes to e2.]]></step>
{% endif %}
{% if sanity_close_mode == "daemon" %}
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Run `atm task close {{ task_id }} completed --template {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/sanity-task-close.md.j2 --vars <selected-vars.json>` immediately, without waiting for any stack result. This is the only close command: do not invoke atm-task-close.py or manually close beads. The registered sanity hook resolves task relationships from current beads and validates PASS/FAIL result shape. FAIL carries its findings exactly as step b selected them, `[{deliverable, issue}]` (never `undone`, `number` or `reason`). PASS and FAIL are the only accepted verdicts. Sanity does not build: missing deliverables or missing/stale dev evidence are FAIL. Assignment conflicts, unavailable required review services, and verification-tool failures require escalation with exact conflicting records or failed operation/error. Legacy CANNOT_RUN is rejected with an explicit lead escalation. Validation errors name an owner and correlation ID; report the error to the phase lead with the failed operation and recovery direction; correct the result or required bead data at its source, then retry close. Bead writes are journaled in bd-cache and applied by its drain; a write that cannot be applied is escalated to the phase lead by the bd-cache cron, so never retry bead writes. For a fixed PASS, only after successful close, prepare stack-input.json with checked_bead, branch, commit, pr_number, worktree_path, and stack_bead/budget/lead from current task/bead context (phase_lead supplies lead); hand that input to sanity-stack. For not_reproducible PASS, skip stacking.]]></step>
{% else %}
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Run {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/sanity-close-vars --manifest <manifest.json> --selected <selected-vars.json> --stack-input <stack-input.json> > <close-vars.json>. Run {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/atm-task-close.py --role sanity --vars <close-vars.json> immediately on the selected verdict, without waiting for any stack result. For a fixed PASS, hand <stack-input.json> unchanged to sanity-stack only after successful close, or run sanity-stack-link --input <stack-input.json> after the close. The generated stack input carries the stack bead and phase lead. For a not_reproducible PASS, no stack input is produced and no stack handoff runs. stack_failed, lock_timeout or rebase_required is notified by sanity-stack-link to the phase lead; this sanity task stays closed and no sanity round is counted for stack outcomes. FAIL retains selected undone numbers and reasons; CANNOT_RUN refuses through the hook. On hook err fix the named cause and rerun with the generated vars; never hand-edit them.]]></step>
{% endif %}
    <step id="e2"><![CDATA[{% if sanity_close_mode == "daemon" %}Do not submit CANNOT_RUN. Missing deliverables or missing/stale evidence are FAIL and return to the dev. For an assignment conflict, required review-service outage, or verification-tool failure, report the exact records or failed operation/error and responsible owner to the phase lead. Keep the task open for that escalation; do not invent a verdict. A bead write that cannot be applied after a validated PASS/FAIL is escalated by bd-cache, not by you; the original task still closes.{% else %}A blocker is not a failure: when a prerequisite reopens or work needs an unlanded fix, never stay active waiting. Record BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why> and any missing edge bd dep add {{ task_id }} --blocked-by <blocker>. Run the legacy hook with verdict CANNOT_RUN; it returns the bead open and unassigned and refuses the task.{% endif %}]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[After the hook closes this task and the post-close stack handoff is dispatched, read ATM again. The console runs tabs replace the chat status table.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
